From: liuqin Fedora adaptation <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] restore the exact-ROM SSC property allowlist

The temporary wildcard experiment did not resolve the SLPI reset. Restore
the original two-property boundary before integrating v0.6.1 continuation
tests. Preserve the write-only/discard file stub; do not expose properties.
---
--- a/hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.c
@@ -28,15 +28,8 @@
 
 static int property_is_allowed(const void *name, size_t len)
 {
-	/*
-	 * Experimental: accept every property name and return an empty value.
-	 * The liuqin firmware enumerates more names than the pinned ROM config;
-	 * rejecting them may abort sensor initialization.  This remains a
-	 * read-only shim and never exposes a generic Android property bridge.
-	 */
-	(void)name;
-	(void)len;
-	return 1;
+	return (len == sizeof(property0) && !memcmp(name, property0, len))
+	    || (len == sizeof(property1) && !memcmp(name, property1, len));
 }
 
 static uint32_t sns_registry_get_property(void *data,
